Job Description
PCB Designer with 6+ years of hands-on experience in Altium Designer to develop high-performance PCB layouts for power electronic and high Speed applications.
Expertise in multilayer PCB design, power supply layouts, DC-DC converters, AC-DC converters, motor control systems, LED drivers, battery management systems, and mixed-signal designs.
Key Responsibilities:
Design and develop 2-layer to 16-layer PCB layouts using Altium Designer and Xpedition at Pune location.
Create and maintain PCB footprints, schematic symbols, and component libraries following IPC standards.
Perform component placement considering thermal, electrical, mechanical, and manufacturability requirements.
Design high-current and high-voltage PCBs with proper creepage and clearance requirements.
Layout power electronics circuits such as: AC/DC Power Supplies, DC/DC Converters, Motor Drives, Battery Charging Systems, LED Drivers and Inverters and Power Control Boards
Implement EMI/EMC design practices during placement and routing.
Perform controlled impedance routing and differential pair routing where required.
Multilayer PCB Design, High Current & High Voltage Layouts, Mixed Signal PCB Design, Thermal Management Techniques, Copper Pour Optimization and HDI, Blind/Buried Vias
Generate manufacturing outputs including: ODB++, IPC-2581, Assembly Drawings, Fabrication Drawings, Pick & Place Files, BOM Documentation.
Conduct design reviews and resolve DFM, DFA, and DFT issues.
Work with PCB fabrication and assembly vendors for successful product realization.
Manage ECOs and design revisions throughout the product lifecycle.
Required Technical Skills: EDA Tools
Altium Designer (Expert Level)
CAM350 / Gerber Viewer Tools
Knowledge of Cadence Allegro or Xpedition is an added advantage.
Educational Qualification
B.E / B.Tech in Electronics & Communication, Electrical & Electronics, Instrumentation or related discipline.
Best Regards,
Kallol Chakraborty
Talent Acquisition
