class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Qualification Criteria - </span><span lang="EN-US">Bachelor's degree or higher in Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, or related field.</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif"></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Mandatory Skills – </span></p><ul type="disc" style="margin-top:0cm"><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst" style="margin-bottom:0cm; margin-left:0cm; line-height:normal"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif">WiFi firmware development – driver, TCP/IP networking (lwIP/Zephyr/net stack/TLS/MQTT) in embedded environment. </span></b></li></ul><ul type="disc" style="margin-top:0cm"><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-bottom:0cm; margin-left:0cm; line-height:normal"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif">Implement and validate WPA2/WPA3-Personal security modes, Protected Management Frames (802.11w) implementation. </span></b></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style="margin-bottom:0cm; margin-left:0cm; line-height:normal"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif">WPA2/WPA3-Enterprise (802.1X/EAP-TLS) – ownership from supplicant configuration to certification.</span></b></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Bill Rate per month for TPC (in terms of INR)- </span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif; color:black">190000</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif; color:black">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Work location - </span><span lang="EN-US">Bangalore / Mysore / Chennai</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif"></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Details JD-</span></p><ul type="disc" style="margin-top:0cm"><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">Strong proficiency in embedded WiFi firmware development: WiFi driver and wpa_supplicant/hostap integration, and TCP/IP networking (lwIP/Zephyr net stack, TLS, MQTT) on resource-constrained devices.</span><span lang="EN-US"></span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">In-depth knowledge of WiFi security and association mechanics: WPA2/WPA3-Personal (SAE), transition mode, PMF (802.11w), 4-way handshake, and scan/connect/reconnect behavior; hands-on WPA2/WPA3 Enterprise (802.1X/EAP-TLS) experience strongly preferred. </span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">Demonstrated experience debugging AP vendor interoperability issues (e.g., Cisco, Aruba, Meraki, Ruckus) using wireless packet capture tools (e.g., Wireshark or specialized sniffer equipment). </span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">Familiarity with enterprise/managed network environments (VLANs, RADIUS, captive portals, client isolation); healthcare IT environments a plus. </span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">Understanding of BLE/WiFi 2.4 GHz coexistence mechanisms and RF fundamentals.</span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">Proficiency in C/C++ and familiarity with assembly language. </span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">&nbsp;Experience with real-time operating systems (RTOS) programming and debug; Zephyr experience preferred. </span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">Knowledge of debugging tools and techniques (e.g., JTAG, oscilloscopes, logic analyzers). </span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">Experience with version control systems (e.g., Git) and issue tracking tools (e.g., Jira). </span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">Strong logical and problem-solving skills. </span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">Good communication and teamwork skills; comfortable interfacing with field teams and customer IT staff. </span></li><li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style="margin-left:0cm"><span lang="EN-US">&nbsp;Experience in NXP RW61x, Silicon Labs, or similar connectivity microcontrollers is preferred</span></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><b><span lang="EN-US">&nbsp;</span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:&quot;Aptos Display&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top:4.0pt"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt; font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif; color:#004B88">Best Regards,</span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top:4.0pt"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt; font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif; color:#004B88">&nbsp;</span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top:4.0pt; line-height:115%"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt; line-height:115%; font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif; color:#004B88">Kallol Chakraborty</span></b></p><p